Subject: [PATCH] validation: close capture ownership gaps around upstream retries

Project-local correctness changes for the pinned validation desktop, on top
of the fully attributed upstream backports 0002 and 0003. These changes are
not represented as an upstream commit.

The fixed 0.8.1 instance destructor frees every timer with user_data == cast.
Clear process_retry before disconnect can synchronously emit UNCONNECTED.
Enter terminal state before normal resource teardown. Register a legacy
capture proxy immediately, since the protocol permits failure before any
wl_shm buffer event and v3 can negotiate only dmabuf. Do not trigger a stream
before creation or after it stopped. Reject incomplete initial constraints
without retaining a dangling frame or partial constraints for another attempt.

The unsupported Y_INVERT path may run inside a PipeWire state callback whose
caller still needs the native stream. Mark the instance terminal, cancel its
frame and retry, and return that outcome to every continuing enqueue caller.
The existing event loop reclaims the instance after all native callbacks
return. Both existing add-buffer failure paths use the same terminal
outcome; subsequent add-buffer notifications allocate nothing. Terminal
instances cannot schedule work through state, format, retry, process or FPS
callbacks. No new timer, thread or ownership framework is added.
This preserves the existing unsupported-frame failure rather than implementing
flipped capture or relaxing any application buffer or first-frame pixel check.

Source identities, checked callback order, scope and verification boundaries
are recorded in upstream.json and docs/portal-wlr-validation.md.
License: MIT, matching the upstream and project licenses.

